<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indian National Army</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Azad Hind Fauj</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indian National Army was a force raised with Japanese support, largely from Indian prisoners of war captured in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, to fight British rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. Revived under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/subhas-chandra-bose">Subhas Chandra Bose</a> in 1943, it served as the army of Azad Hind and fought in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imphal">Imphal</a> and Kohima campaign of 1944. The trials of its officers in 1945–1946 stirred nationalist feeling across India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/indian-national-army.jpg" alt="Indian National Army" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adiiitya · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:INA_Insignia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
